Parked — spelling RULED 2026-10-24, but blocked on implementation gaps
that are NOT the ruling.

The tag question this test carried is settled: the kind is declared once on
the parameter (`source: Source[HTML]` — a compiler annotation in the `[]`
lane), and the call site never echoes it — this test's `[HTML]{` invocation
was respelled to a bare `{`. The `<T>{` typed-block and `<T>"path"` typed
file-source forms are removed entirely (PARSE001 refusals teach the
migration).

What still blocks green (unchanged by the ruling, from the 2026-06-03 walk):
- Emitter: panics on a source-block invocation in CONTINUATION position;
  every green source-block test invokes at top level.
- Transform: this test's own ~470-line hand-rolled transform walks
  `flow.continuations` assuming a top-level flow shape and mis-attaches
  `| rendered` when renderHTML sits as a nested continuation body.
